----------------
Step1X-3D — https://github.com/stepfun-ai/Step1X-3D — Apache License 2.0.
Forked at commit cb5ac94 ("[Fix] fix bug in sharp edge sampling").

Removed from this fork
----------------------
The upstream texture stack and one geometry file carried a verbatim
"TENCENT HUNYUAN NON-COMMERCIAL LICENSE AGREEMENT" header. They are not part of
this fork:

- step1x3d_texture/** (the whole texture pipeline, including the vendored
  custom_rasterizer and differentiable_renderer extensions), configs/
  train-texture-ig2mv/**, data/ig2mv/**, train_ig2mv.py and train_ig2mv.sh —
  deleted.
- step1x3d_geometry/models/autoencoders/volume_decoders.py — replaced by an
  independent implementation written for this fork against the interface the
  geometry VAE requires. See FORK.md and tests/test_volume_decoders.py.

Third-party code retained in this fork
--------------------------------------
The geometry stack contains files adapted from, or citing, the following
projects. Their own licences continue to apply to those portions:

- Hugging Face Diffusers and Transformers — Apache License 2.0
  (step1x3d_geometry/models/transformers/*, models/conditional_encoders/*).
- facebookresearch/dino and facebookresearch/dinov2 — Apache License 2.0
  (models/conditional_encoders/dinov2*).
- openai/CLIP — MIT License (models/conditional_encoders/clip*).
- PixArt-alpha/PixArt-alpha — Apache License 2.0 (referenced in
  models/attention.py and models/transformers/pixart_transformer_1d.py).
- 3DTopia/OpenLRM — Apache License 2.0 (referenced in the conditional
  encoders).
- facebookresearch/DiT — Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International. Listed in
  the "Reference:" comment of
  models/conditional_encoders/clip/modeling_conditional_clip.py and
  models/conditional_encoders/dinov2/modeling_conditional_dinov2.py. Both files
  carry the Apache-2.0 header of the Hugging Face Transformers model files they
  adapt, and neither contains the adaLN-Zero block that the cited DiT region
  implements: there is no modulate(), adaLN, shift_msa or scale_msa code in
  models/conditional_encoders/. The reference is therefore an architectural
  citation rather than copied expression. See FORK.md for the exact check.

